        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "43d99153-782e-5b86-9bf8-95e00a9cc5dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joni Mitchell, Sara Bareilles\n- Products: Both Sides Now, \"Both Sides, Now\", Love Actually\n- Events: Grammy Awards, 89th Academy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- \"Both Sides, Now\" is a song by Joni Mitchell and is one of her best-known songs.\n- Joni Mitchell re-recorded \"Both Sides, Now\" in an orchestrated version for her 2000 album Both Sides Now.\n- The album Both Sides Now won two Grammy Awards in 2001: Best Traditional Pop Vocal Album and Best Instrumental Arrangement Accompanying Vocalist(s) for the song \"Both Sides, Now\".\n- Joni Mitchell's orchestrated version of \"Both Sides, Now\" was later featured on the soundtrack of the 2003 film Love Actually.\n- Sara Bareilles performed \"Both Sides, Now\" during the 89th Academy Awards' In Memoriam homage.",
